umbbells, espresso, flagship, headphones, home-gym, kitchen, laptop, lighting, massage, muscle, noise-cancelling, portable, premium, professional, recovery, smart-equipment, smart-home, smartphone, strength, subscription, therapy, vacuum, weights, wireless) that does NOT include \\\"qa-newtag\\\", even though the product carrying that tag exists and is searchable by keyword. The tag-filter chip list appears to be a static/precomputed set rather than derived from current product tags.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Used Admin \\\"Add Product\\\" form to create \\\"QA Fitness Gadget\\\" (Category: Fitness, tag: \\\"qa-createtag\\\"); toast confirmed \\\"Product created successfully\\\" and it appeared in /admin and /products lists (11 products found, up from 9). Searching \\\"qa-createtag\\\" on /products correctly returned exactly that 1 new product, confirming new tags assigned at creation are immediately usable for search/filtering.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited Apple MacBook Pro 14\\\" tags to add \\\"qa-newtag\\\"; saved successfully. Product detail page displayed the new tag alongside existing ones, and searching \\\"qa-newtag\\\" on /products returned exactly that product (1 product found).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"The Create/Edit product Category field is a single-select combobox (listbox with options Tech Gadgets / Home Goods / Fitness) - only one can be chosen at a time, enforcing single-category assignment. Selecting \\\"Fitness\\\" for the new \\\"QA Fitness Gadget\\\" product correctly assigned and displayed it under the Fitness category badge in both /admin and /products listings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On /products, opened Category combobox and selected \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\": results instantly updated to show exactly the 3 tech products (Sony WH-1000XM5, Samsung Galaxy S24 Ultra, Apple MacBook Pro 14\\\") without a page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"On /products, all 9 seeded products render as cards each showing: image, name (linked), category badge (Tech/Home/Fitness), price, star rating with numeric value, a brief review/description paragraph, and a \\\"Buy Now\\\" purchase action link to an external retailer URL.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sort \\\"Price: Low to High\\\" on Tech Gadgets category correctly ordered Sony $399 -> Samsung $1299 -> MacBook $1999. Minimum Rating filter \\\"4.5+ stars\\\" applied across All Categories correctly reduced 9->8 products, excluding exactly Philips Hue Starter Kit (rated 4.4), the only product below the threshold.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Edits not persisted server-side; lost on reload\", \"actual\": \"After editing Sony WH-1000XM5 (price 399->375, rating 4.8->4.9, description, tags, full review, added a spec) and saving successfully, a full page navigation/reload to /admin, /products, and /product/sony-wh-1000xm5 reverted all fields back to the original seeded values ($399, 4.8, original description/tags/review, no new spec). Changes only survive within the current in-memory SPA session and are lost on reload/revisit.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Reviewed all product cards in /admin: each of the original 9 seeded products plus 2 newly created products shows exactly one category badge (Tech, Home, or Fitness) - no product displayed multiple or zero category badges. The category selector UI is single-select only, structurally enforcing exactly one category per product.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined-criteria checks: (1) selecting tags \\\"apple\\\"+\\\"headphones\\\" (OR logic) returned exactly 2 products, each carrying at least one selected tag. (2) Category \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\" + Sort \\\"Price: Low to High\\\" correctly returned only the 3 tech products ordered Sony $399 -> Samsung $1299 -> MacBook $1999. (3) Minimum Rating \\\"4.5+ stars\\\" across All Categories + Sort \\\"Price: Low to High\\\" correctly reduced 9->8 products (excluding only Philips Hue Starter Kit at 4.4) while remaining price-sorted. All displayed results satisfied every simultaneously active criterion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Publish validation incomplete: allows saving products missing required fields and lacks explicit invalid-value feedback\", \"actual\": \"Only Product Name, Category, and Short Description are enforced as required (submitting with all three blank shows toast \\\"Please fill in all required fields\\\" and blocks creation). However, submitting with Name/Category/Description filled but Image URL, Affiliate Link, Full Review, and Specifications left completely empty succeeded (\\\"Product created successfully\\\"), producing a live product (\\\"QA Test Product\\\", later \\\"QA Fitness Gadget\\\") with no image, an empty Buy Now link (href=\\\"\\\"), no full review, and no specs - violating the requirement that image, a valid retailer link, and at least one complete spec be required to publish. Additionally, entering an out-of-range price (-50) and rating (7, outside 0-5) silently prevented submission with no error toast or inline message explaining why, giving the user no feedback on what was invalid.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Navigating to /product/nonexistent-product-xyz shows \\\"Product Not Found\\\" heading with explanatory text and a \\\"Browse All Products\\\" link. Navigating to /category/nonexistent-category-xyz shows \\\"Category Not Found\\\" heading with explanatory text. Both invalid-ID routes render graceful not-found states instead of crashing or showing blank/broken UI.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Across multiple filter/sort interactions on /products (keyword search \\\"qa-newtag\\\", tag chip selection, category combobox selection, sort combobox selection, minimum rating combobox selection), results updated live/instantly in the DOM without any browser_navigate or page reload being required.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Product card image and name are both wrapped in links pointing to the matching /product/{slug} URL (e.g., Sony WH-1000XM5 image link and name link both point to /product/sony-wh-1000xm5); clicking either previously navigated correctly to that product's detail page.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each product card's \\\"Buy Now\\\" link points to a distinct external retailer URL (e.g., https://example.com/sony-xm5, https://example.com/macbook-pro, https://example.com/peloton), consistent with opening an external retailer page rather than an internal route.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Selecting \\\"Tech Gadgets\\\" in the Category combobox immediately updated the active category state and the displayed product grid to the 3 matching products, with no full page reload/navigation required.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sony WH-1000XM5 detail page (/product/sony-wh-1000xm5) displays all expected fields: image, category (Tech), star rating (4.8), name, description, price ($399), Buy Now external link, tag chips (headphones, wireless, noise-cancelling, premium), a \\\"Key Specifications\\\" block with 5 specs (Driver Size, Battery Life, Weight, Bluetooth, Noise Cancelling), and a full untruncated \\\"My Review\\\" paragraph.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Seeded products consistently use category/tag values relevant to their nature: Sony WH-1000XM5 (Tech) tagged headphones/wireless/noise-cancelling/premium; MacBook Pro (Tech) implicitly laptop/apple/premium per earlier filter-chip list; fitness items (Bowflex, Theragun, Peloton) fall under Fitness category; home items (Breville, Philips Hue, Dyson) fall under Home. No mismatched category/tag combinations observed across products browsed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sony WH-1000XM5 fields matched exactly between /products list card and its detail page: category \\\"Tech\\\", price \\\"$399\\\", rating \\\"4.8\\\", and description text \\\"Industry-leading noise cancellation with exceptional sound quality and all-day comfort.\\\" identical in both views. Detail page additionally shows the full untruncated review and complete specs list, consistent with the shortened card-view summary.\"}]}"
